  "result": "I've fixed it: `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now returns a value inside the range. The relevant tests pass (71 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/click/types.py:754`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. The old code stepped one past the open bound, outside the range.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_types.py`:\n  - `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `\"-5\"` now returns `1` (it used to return `-1`).\n  - `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `\"10\"` now returns `4` (it used to return `6`).\n\nI ran `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py`, not the full test suite. Nothing is committed.",
